/*
** CNet/4 Who CGI Documentation
** by Kelly Cochran
** Last Change: Sun Nov 30 19:39:56 1997
*/

Purpose:

    This utility allows you to have a web page display the current users
online your system.

Requirments:

    A TCP stack (AmiTCP or Miami preferrable)
    A web server (AWS preferred, but it will work it apache as well if you make
      an AWS: assign to accomodate the placement of the conf file)
    CNet/4 (any version after 4.13)

Features:

    Simple to install and configure.
    All output text is configurable in color, and layout.

Installation:

    Installation of who-cgi is simple.  Just copy the files in the archive to
the appropriate places in your AWS: directory.  Edit the who.conf file as you
like, but be careful (as with bbstext) to not delete any lines, unless they are
the lines controlling files to be output, and where to stick the who in that list

    Tada!  It's installed.

Usage:

    Just use any web browser to access http://your.site.com/cgi-bin/who

